Django notes:

1.“Real-world APIs use GET to fetch data, POST to create data, PUT/PATCH to update, DELETE to remove data, while webhooks handle push-based real-time events like payments and messages.”
2.“A webhook in Django is an HTTP endpoint that receives real-time event data from external services using POST requests. It is used for payment notifications, message events, and third-party integrations.”

 API                   | Webhook            |
| -------------------- | ------------------ |
| Client requests data | Server pushes data |
| Pull model           | Push model         |
| Not real-time        | Real-time          |

