WebHook - A webhook is an HTTP callback that allows one system to send real-time data to another system when an event occurs using POST requests.
Why is @csrf_exempt used in webhooks? - External services cannot send CSRF tokens, so CSRF protection must be disabled for webhook endpoints.
How do you secure a webhook?
Signature verification
Secret key validation
